Dynamic age-dependent PBPK model for 6:2 Cl-PFESA (F-53B)
; Chinese male piecewise-linear height and weight with direct age-dependent physiology
; PRIMARY USE:
; Adult-life-course exposure from age 20 years to age 79 years.
; MODELING STRATEGY:
; 1. Use Chinese male age-group height and body-weight data with
; piecewise-linear interpolation.
; 2. Insert the Chinese anthropometry directly into published male
; organ-volume and cardiac-output equations, without 25-y/65-y anchoring.
; 3. Keep F-53B-specific partition coefficients, protein binding,
; absorption and transporter parameters constant with age.
; 4. Htc is fixed at 0.44 and FVBK at 0.24. GFRC is derived from
; age-specific eGFR, BSA, and kidney volume.
; 5. From age 20 through 50 y, organ blood-flow fractions are fixed at:
; QBC=0.12, QKC=0.19, and QLC=0.255.
; After age 50 y, these fractions decline according to the published
; male age-specific organ-flow shapes, normalized to the age-50 values.
; 6. Exposure is age-stratified according to daily energy intake.
; IMPORTANT:
; This is an adult-life-course model, not a validated birth-to-old-age model.
; Maternal transfer, lactation, childhood renal maturation and child-specific
; exposure pathways are not represented.
; UNITS:
; Time: h
; Amount: mg
; Concentration: mg/L
; With brain density approximated as 1 kg/L:
; 1 mg/L = 1 ug/g = 1000 ng/g
; 1. TIME AND AGE
Starttime = 0
Age_start_year = 20
Age_end_year   = 65
T65 = 394200
Stoptime = 394200
DTMIN = 1e-7
DTMAX = 1
DTOUT = 24
TOLERANCE = 0.0000001
Age_year = Age_start_year + TIME/(365*24)
; 2. CHINESE MALE HEIGHT AND BODY WEIGHT
; Piecewise-linear interpolation of age-group means
; Age midpoint (y): 22.5  27.5  32.5  37.5  42.5  47.5
; Height (cm):      172.6 172.1 171.4 170.4 169.4 168.7
; BW (kg):           70.4  72.8  74.3  74.0  73.2  72.5
 
; Age midpoint (y): 52.5  57.5  62.5  67.5  72.5  77.5
; Height (cm):      167.9 167.5 165.9 165.4 164.6 164.2
; BW (kg):           71.6  71.0  69.0  68.1  66.7  65.0
; Ages below 22.5 y use the 20-24 y group mean.
; Ages above 77.5 y use the 75-79 y group mean.
BW = IF Age_year <= 22.5 THEN 70.4 ELSE IF Age_year <= 27.5 THEN
70.4+(72.8-70.4)*(Age_year-22.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 32.5 THEN
72.8+(74.3-72.8)*(Age_year-27.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 37.5 THEN
74.3+(74.0-74.3)*(Age_year-32.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 42.5 THEN
74.0+(73.2-74.0)*(Age_year-37.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 47.5 THEN
73.2+(72.5-73.2)*(Age_year-42.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 52.5 THEN
72.5+(71.6-72.5)*(Age_year-47.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 57.5 THEN
71.6+(71.0-71.6)*(Age_year-52.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 62.5 THEN
71.0+(69.0-71.0)*(Age_year-57.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 67.5 THEN
69.0+(68.1-69.0)*(Age_year-62.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 72.5 THEN
68.1+(66.7-68.1)*(Age_year-67.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 77.5 THEN
66.7+(65.0-66.7)*(Age_year-72.5)/5 ELSE 65.0
HT = IF Age_year <= 22.5 THEN 172.6 ELSE IF Age_year <= 27.5 THEN
172.6+(172.1-172.6)*(Age_year-22.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 32.5 THEN
172.1+(171.4-172.1)*(Age_year-27.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 37.5 THEN
171.4+(170.4-171.4)*(Age_year-32.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 42.5 THEN
170.4+(169.4-170.4)*(Age_year-37.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 47.5 THEN
169.4+(168.7-169.4)*(Age_year-42.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 52.5 THEN
168.7+(167.9-168.7)*(Age_year-47.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 57.5 THEN
167.9+(167.5-167.9)*(Age_year-52.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 62.5 THEN
167.5+(165.9-167.5)*(Age_year-57.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 67.5 THEN
165.9+(165.4-165.9)*(Age_year-62.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 72.5 THEN
165.4+(164.6-165.4)*(Age_year-67.5)/5 ELSE IF Age_year <= 77.5 THEN
164.6+(164.2-164.6)*(Age_year-72.5)/5 ELSE 164.2
; 3. AGE-DEPENDENT MALE ORGAN VOLUMES
; The published male regression equations are used directly with the
; interpolated Chinese male age, BW and HT.
; No 25-y or 65-y organ-volume scale factors are applied.
; These outputs are best described as:
; "organ volumes predicted by published male equations using
; Chinese male age-specific anthropometry".
; Liver volume, L
VL = -0.0143744 -0.0044728*Age_year +0.0264591*BW
; Brain volume, L
VB = 0.218096 -0.001590*Age_year -0.003274*BW +0.008626*HT
; Kidney volume, L
VK = 0.05668 -0.0004962*Age_year +0.003501*BW
; Lung volume, L
VLu = -0.01454 +0.0007269*Age_year +9.329E-6*Age_year^2 +0.006430*BW +3.083E-5*BW^2
 
; 4. AGE-DEPENDENT MALE CARDIAC OUTPUT
; Chinese male HT and BW are used in the Du Bois body-surface-area equation.
; The published male cardiac-output equation is then used directly.
; No cardiac-output anchoring scale is applied.
SA = 0.007184*(BW^0.425)*(HT^0.725)
QC_blood = 6.48370 -1.59948*Age_year +214.68572*SA
; 5. OTHER PHYSIOLOGICAL PARAMETERS
; Htc and FVBK are fixed as requested. Organ-specific blood flows are
; calculated below from published age-shape data anchored to Chinese
; adult male age-50 flow fractions.
; Hematocrit fixed as requested
Htc = 0.44
VPlasC = 0.0428
VPlas = VPlasC*BW
; Filtrate volume is maintained at approximately 10% of kidney volume.
Vfil = 0.10*VK
VPTCC = 0.000135
VPTC = VK*VPTCC
; Kidney blood-volume fraction fixed as requested
FVBK = 0.24
VKb = VK*FVBK
; AGE-DEPENDENT ORGAN BLOOD FLOWS
; Requested modeling assumption:
; 20-50 y:
; QBC = 0.12
; QKC = 0.19
; QLC = 0.255
; >50 y:
; Each fraction is reduced according to the published age-specific
; whole-blood organ-flow shape relative to the published age-50 value.
; Therefore:
; QBC(age) = 0.12  * [QB_ref(age)/QB_ref(50)]   for age > 50
; QKC(age) = 0.19  * [QK_ref(age)/QK_ref(50)]   for age > 50
; QLC(age) = 0.255 * [QL_ref(age)/QL_ref(50)]   for age > 50
; Published male age-specific WHOLE-BLOOD organ flows (mL/min):
; Brain:
; age 50  727.9
; age 60  692.9
; age 70  650.6
; age 80  623.8
; age 90  594.4
; age 100 536.1
; Kidney:
; age 50  1116.3
; age 60  913.3
; age 70   730.3
; age 80   567.3
; age 90   424.3
; age 100  301.3
; Total liver:
; age 50  1661.6
; age 60  1418.6
; age 70  1091.6
; age 80   819.7
; age 90   688.6
; age 100  555.1
; 50-y reference flow fractions
QBC50 = 0.12
QKC50 = 0.19
QLC50 = 0.255
; Published brain blood-flow shape
; For age <=50, factor is fixed at 1.
QB_ref_mL_min = IF Age_year <= 50 THEN 727.9 ELSE IF Age_year <= 60 THEN
727.9+(692.9-727.9)*(Age_year-50)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 70 THEN
692.9+(650.6-692.9)*(Age_year-60)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 80 THEN
650.6+(623.8-650.6)*(Age_year-70)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 90 THEN
623.8+(594.4-623.8)*(Age_year-80)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 100 THEN
594.4+(536.1-594.4)*(Age_year-90)/10 ELSE 536.1
QB_age_factor = QB_ref_mL_min/727.9
 
; Published kidney blood-flow shape
; For age <=50, factor is fixed at 1.
QK_ref_mL_min = IF Age_year <= 50 THEN 1116.3 ELSE IF Age_year <= 60 THEN
1116.3+(913.3-1116.3)*(Age_year-50)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 70 THEN
913.3+(730.3-913.3)*(Age_year-60)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 80 THEN
730.3+(567.3-730.3)*(Age_year-70)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 90 THEN
567.3+(424.3-567.3)*(Age_year-80)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 100 THEN
424.3+(301.3-424.3)*(Age_year-90)/10 ELSE 301.3
QK_age_factor = QK_ref_mL_min/1116.3
; Published total liver blood-flow shape
; For age <=50, factor is fixed at 1.
QL_ref_mL_min = IF Age_year <= 50 THEN 1661.6 ELSE IF Age_year <= 60 THEN
1661.6+(1418.6-1661.6)*(Age_year-50)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 70 THEN
1418.6+(1091.6-1418.6)*(Age_year-60)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 80 THEN
1091.6+(819.7-1091.6)*(Age_year-70)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 90 THEN
819.7+(688.6-819.7)*(Age_year-80)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 100 THEN
688.6+(555.1-688.6)*(Age_year-90)/10 ELSE 555.1
QL_age_factor = QL_ref_mL_min/1661.6
; Dynamic age-specific flow fractions
QBC = QBC50*QB_age_factor
QKC = QKC50*QK_age_factor
QLC = QLC50*QL_age_factor
QLuC = 1
; Dynamic whole-blood organ flows
; Current organ fractions are applied to current whole-blood cardiac output.
QB_blood = QBC*QC_blood
QK_blood = QKC*QC_blood
QL_blood = QLC*QC_blood
; Convert whole-blood flows to plasma flows used by PBPK equations
QC = QC_blood*(1-Htc)
QB = QB_blood*(1-Htc)
QK = QK_blood*(1-Htc)
QL = QL_blood*(1-Htc)
QLu = QC
QRest = QC-QL-QK-QB
; AGE-SPECIFIC RENAL FILTRATION
; eGFR data supplied by the user:
; 20-29 y: 113.94 mL/min/1.73 m2
; 30-39 y: 106.93 mL/min/1.73 m2
; 40-49 y: 100.31 mL/min/1.73 m2
; 50-59 y:  96.32 mL/min/1.73 m2
; 60-69 y:  88.63 mL/min/1.73 m2
; 70-79 y:  82.76 mL/min/1.73 m2
; For ages 20-69, group means are assigned to the midpoint of each
; 10-y age band (24.5, 34.5, 44.5, 54.5, 64.5 y), with piecewise-linear
; interpolation between adjacent midpoints.
; The current simulation extends to age 79 years, so the >=70-y eGFR
; information is used in the present simulation.
eGFR = IF Age_year <= 24.5 THEN 113.94 ELSE IF Age_year <= 34.5 THEN
113.94+(106.93-113.94)*(Age_year-24.5)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 44.5 THEN
106.93+(100.31-106.93)*(Age_year-34.5)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 54.5 THEN
100.31+(96.32-100.31)*(Age_year-44.5)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 64.5 THEN
96.32+(88.63-96.32)*(Age_year-54.5)/10 ELSE IF Age_year <= 74.5 THEN
88.63+(82.76-88.63)*(Age_year-64.5)/10 ELSE 82.76
; Convert indexed eGFR to absolute GFR using dynamic BSA.
GFR_mL_min = eGFR*SA/1.73
; mL/min
GFR = GFR_mL_min*60/1000
; L/h
; Derive the PBPK filtration coefficient.
; Kidney density is treated as approximately 1 kg/L, so VK (L)
; is numerically used as kidney mass (kg).
GFRC = GFR/VK
; L/h/kg kidney
; Constant physiological parameters
GEC = 3.5
protein = 2.0E-6
; Remaining body volume
VRest = 0.93*BW -VL -VLu -VB -VK -VPlas -VPTC -Vfil
; Diagnostic fractional volumes and equivalent cardiac-output scalar
VLC = VL/BW
VKC = VK/BW
VLuC = VLu/BW
VBC = VB/BW
VfilC = Vfil/BW
QCC_equiv = QC_blood/(BW^0.75)
; 6. F-53B-SPECIFIC PARAMETERS
; These parameters are kept constant with age.
; They come from the user's F-53B model or its human extrapolation.
; The PFOS lifetime paper is used for the age-shape of physiology, not to
; replace F-53B-specific chemistry.
PL =13.59
PK =1.38
PLu =3.91
PB = 0.11
PRest = 0.32
MW = 532.58
Free = 0.0043
Vmax_baso_invitro = 479
Km_baso = 20.1
Vmax_apical_invitro = 51803
Km_apical = 64.4
RAFbaso = 1
RAFapi = 0.001
Kdif =0.001
KabsC = 0.066
KunabsC = 0.000421
K0C = 0.38
KeffluxC =2.09
; Keep the same base elimination constants across age.
; Age effects enter through BW, organ volume, GFR and transporter capacity.
KbileC = 0.0001
KurineC = 0.000016
HL_day = 5588
; 7. DERIVED KINETIC PARAMETERS
MK = VK*1000
; Number of proximal-tubule cells per kg BW
PTC_cells_perkg = VKC*1000*6E7
MPTC = VPTC*1000
Vmax_basoC = Vmax_baso_invitro *RAFbaso *PTC_cells_perkg *protein *60 *(MW/1E12) *1000
Vmax_apicalC = Vmax_apical_invitro *RAFapi *PTC_cells_perkg *protein *60 *(MW/1E12) *1000
Vmax_baso = Vmax_basoC*(BW^0.75)
Vmax_apical = Vmax_apicalC*(BW^0.75)
Kbile = KbileC*(BW^-0.25)
Kurine = KurineC*(BW^-0.25)
Kefflux = KeffluxC*(BW^-0.25)
Kabs = KabsC*(BW^-0.25)
Kunabs = KunabsC*(BW^-0.25)
GE = GEC*(BW^-0.25)
K0 = K0C*(BW^-0.25)
; Hepatic clearance
; Convert the human half-life from days to hours before comparing with QL.
Vd = (PL*VL +PK*VK +PLu*VLu +PB*VB +PRest*VRest) +VPlas
Cle_h = 0.693/(HL_day*24)*Vd
Clint_h_per_Liver = (Cle_h/(1-Cle_h/QL))/VL
Eh = Clint_h_per_Liver*VL /(Clint_h_per_Liver*VL+QL)
; 7A. INITIAL BACKGROUND BODY BURDEN AT AGE 20
; Plasma F-53B concentration at model start = 0.57 ng/mL.
; 0.57 ng/mL = 0.00057 mg/L.
; Major perfusion-limited tissues are initialized using the model partition
; coefficients to avoid an artificial zero-tissue redistribution transient:
; C_tissue,0 = P_tissue * C_plasma,0
; These are model-derived equilibrium initial conditions, not measured
; human organ concentrations.
C0_plasma_ng_mL = 0.57
C0_plasma_mg_L = C0_plasma_ng_mL/1000
C0_liver_mg_L = PL*C0_plasma_mg_L
C0_kidney_mg_L = PK*C0_plasma_mg_L
C0_lung_mg_L = PLu*C0_plasma_mg_L
C0_brain_mg_L = PB*C0_plasma_mg_L
C0_rest_mg_L = PRest*C0_plasma_mg_L
; 8. AGE-STRATIFIED ENVIRONMENTAL EXPOSURE
; Exposure is scaled in direct proportion to age-specific daily energy intake.
; Reference:
; age 18-<50 y: 2600 kcal/day -> 0.122 ng/kg/day
; Scaled exposure:
; age 50-<65 y: 2450/2600 of reference
;                 = 0.114962 ng/kg/day
;                 = 1.14961538E-07 mg/kg/day
 
;   age 65-80 y:  2350/2600 of reference
;                 = 0.110269 ng/kg/day
;                 = 1.10269231E-07 mg/kg/day
; The present model starts at age 20 y, so the 18-<50 y category is applied
; from age 20 to <50 y. Exposure changes stepwise at ages 50 and 65.
Dose18_50_mgkgd = 1.22E-7
Dose50_65_mgkgd = Dose18_50_mgkgd*(2450/2600)
Dose65_80_mgkgd = Dose18_50_mgkgd*(2350/2600)
Dose_mgkgd = IF Age_year < 50 THEN Dose18_50_mgkgd ELSE IF Age_year < 65 THEN Dose50_65_mgkgd ELSE Dose65_80_mgkgd
DOSEF53B = Dose_mgkgd*BW
doseF53B_int = 24
ADOSE' = pulse(DOSEF53B,0,doseF53B_int)
Init ADOSE = 0
; 9. CONCENTRATIONS
CA_free = RA_free/(VPlas*0.2)
CV_free = RV_free/(VPlas*0.8)
CA = CA_free/Free
CV = CV_free/Free
Cplas = ((RA_free+RV_free)/VPlas)/Free
CL = RL/VL
CVL = CL/PL
CKb = RKb/VKb
CVK = CKb
CK = CVK*PK
CLu = RLu/VLu
CVLu = CLu/PLu
CB = RB/VB
CVB = CB/PB
CRest = RRest/VRest
CVRest = CRest/PRest
CPTC = RPTC/VPTC
Cfil = RFil/Vfil
; 10. INSTANTANEOUS RENAL TRANSPORT RATES
Rate_baso = (Vmax_baso*CKb)/(Km_baso+CKb)
Rate_apical = (Vmax_apical*Cfil)/(Km_apical+Cfil)
Rate_dif = Kdif*(CKb - CPTC)
Rate_efflux = Kefflux*RPTC
Rate_GFR = CA*GFR*Free
; Optional cumulative diagnostics
Cum_baso' = Rate_baso
Init Cum_baso = 0
Cum_apical' = Rate_apical
Init Cum_apical = 0
Cum_dif' = Rate_dif
Init Cum_dif = 0
Cum_efflux' = Rate_efflux
Init Cum_efflux = 0
Cum_GFR' = Rate_GFR
Init Cum_GFR = 0
; 11. DIFFERENTIAL EQUATIONS
; Venous free plasma
RV_free' = (QRest*CVRest*Free) +(QK*CVK*Free) +(QL*CVL*Free) +(QB*CVB*Free) -(QLu*CV*Free) +Rate_efflux
Init RV_free = C0_plasma_mg_L*Free*VPlas*0.8
; Arterial free plasma
RA_free' = (QLu*CVLu*Free) -(QC*CA*Free)
Init RA_free = C0_plasma_mg_L*Free*VPlas*0.2
; Proximal tubule cells
RPTC' = Rate_dif +Rate_apical +Rate_baso -Rate_efflux
Init RPTC = 0
; PTC background burden is not directly inferred from plasma.
; Filtrate
Rfil' = Rate_GFR -Rate_apical -RFil*Kurine
Init Rfil = 0
; Filtrate background burden is not directly inferred from plasma.
; Urine
Rurine' = Kurine*RFil
Init Rurine = 0
; Kidney blood/tissue compartment
RKb' = QK*(CA-CVK)*Free -Rate_GFR -Rate_dif -Rate_baso
Init RKb = C0_plasma_mg_L*VKb
; Rest of body
RRest' = QRest*(CA-CVRest)*Free
Init RRest = C0_rest_mg_L*VRest
; Lung
RLu' = QLu*(CV-CVLu)*Free
Init RLu = C0_lung_mg_L*VLu
; Brain
RB' = QB*(CA-CVB)*Free
Init RB = C0_brain_mg_L*VB
; Stomach
RST' = pulse(DOSEF53B,0,doseF53B_int) -K0*RST -GE*RST
Init RST = 0
RabsST' = K0*RST
Init RabsST = 0
; Cumulative biliary transfer
Rbile' = Kbile*RL
Init Rbile = 0
; Small intestine with enterohepatic return
RSI' = GE*RST -Kabs*RSI -Kunabs*RSI +Kbile*RL
Init RSI = 0
RabsSI' = Kabs*RSI
Init RabsSI = 0
Total_oral_uptake = RabsSI+RabsST
; Feces
Rfeces' = Kunabs*RSI
Init Rfeces = 0
; Hepatic metabolism
Rmeta' = Eh*QL*CA*Free
Init Rmeta = 0
; Liver
RL' = QL*(CA-CVL)*Free -Kbile*RL -Eh*QL*CA*Free +Kabs*RSI +K0*RST
Init RL = C0_liver_mg_L*VL
; 12. MASS BALANCE
Qbal = QC-QL-QK-QRest-QB
Tmass = RA_free +RV_free +RRest +RKb +RFil +RPTC +RL +RST +RSI +RLu +RB
Loss = Rurine +Rfeces +Rmeta
; Initial model-state burden at age 20.
Initial_body_burden' = 0
INIT Initial_body_burden = (C0_plasma_mg_L*Free*VPlas) +(C0_rest_mg_L*VRest) +(C0_plasma_mg_L*VKb) +(C0_liver_mg_L*VL) +(C0_lung_mg_L*VLu) +(C0_brain_mg_L*VB)
Input = Initial_body_burden+ADOSE
Bal = Input-Tmass-Loss
; Instantaneous brain concentration
Brain = RB/VB
